#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.10"
# dependencies = ["mlx", "huggingface_hub"]
# ///
"""
waldito -- small machines making small contributions to openwaldo models

Waldo is the tooling, the corpora index, the bill of materials, and systems to manage it all.
Waldito, as the diminutive of waldo, aims to create the simplest possible waldo that can possibly work.

Setup: `brew install uv`; `./waldito` then runs in a cached environment with mlx and huggingface_hub.

Compose files are written by hand or with AI from what catalog shows -- see docs/MODEL-COMPOSE.md.

Repeated runs: `waldo config set lookaside.cache.keep true` skips re-downloading shards (LRU-bounded by
lookaside.cache.max-size); `waldo lookaside cache status` to inspect, `waldo lookaside cache clean` when done.

Usage:
    waldito catalog                             # every corpus in the index (fiction, caselaw, ...)
    waldito catalog code/*                      # ...narrowed to corpora matching a glob
    waldito catalog code/* --code               # languages and repo counts merged across that glob
    waldito catalog --code --lang python,typescript              # specify specific programming_languages
    waldito catalog code/permissive --code --lang typescript     # ...just within that one corpus
    waldito merge merged/ a-hf/ b-hf/           # average huggingface exports that share a parent
    waldito hub ~/hub                           # serve ~/hub/<org>/<repo>/ to `waldo model pull` via HF_ENDPOINT
    waldito ingest ../fetchers/corpora/x.ini post-train/sft/x   # committed local data -> local test index
    waldito check my-model evaluation.jsonl     # exact-match score of `model chat` against prompt/response rows
    waldito build waldito-python-basics         # plans/<name>.yaml: distributed build with replicas, merges, checks
    waldito join ~/runs.git runs/tiny --identity alice   # one identity's turns in a run kept in git: train, verify, merge
    waldito train python-basics-v2              # ~/.waldo/waldito/python-basics-v2.yaml: generate, ingest --dev, train, check
"""
